module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.SmallSite.Cohomology
public import StacksFrontier.Cotangent.ThreefoldPolynomialSite

/-!
# The chaotic subsite of thickenings of the whole space

Fix a global crystalline situation `(p, (S, I, γ), X)`.  Among the objects `(U, T, δ)` of the
small crystalline site `Cris(X/S)` are those with `U = X`, the whole space: the structure map
`U ⟶ X` of an object of `Cris(X/S)` is an open immersion, and `U = X` says that this open
immersion is an isomorphism.  They span a full subcategory `𝒞 ⊆ Cris(X/S)`, and
[Stacks, Tag 07JK] endows it with the *chaotic* topology of [Stacks, Tag 07GE], for which every
presheaf is a sheaf.

This file constructs that site, the inclusion `𝒞 ⟶ Cris(X/S)`, the restriction functor
`F ↦ F|_𝒞` on abelian sheaves and the cohomology groups `H^j(𝒞, -)`.  The comparison asserted
by [Stacks, Tag 07JK] is not proved here; it is
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite.chaoticCohomologyComparisonIso`.

## Main definitions

Everything below lives in the namespace `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite`.

* `IsOverWholeSpace` — the property cutting out the subcategory: the structure map `U ⟶ X` is an
  isomorphism, i.e. `U = X`.
* `WholeSpaceThickening` — the objects of `𝒞`, the full subcategory of `Cris(X/S)` they span,
  and `wholeι` the inclusion `𝒞 ⥤ Cris(X/S)`.
* `chaoticTopology` — the chaotic topology on `𝒞`, the bottom Grothendieck topology, in which
  only the maximal sieve covers.
* `sheafEquivPresheaf` — sheaves on `𝒞` are the presheaves on `𝒞`, the second assertion of
  [Stacks, Tag 07GE].
* `restrictToWhole` — the restriction `F ↦ F|_𝒞` of an abelian sheaf on `Cris(X/S)` to `𝒞`.
* `chaoticGlobalSections`, `chaoticCohomologyFunctor`, `chaoticCohomology` — global sections and
  the cohomology groups `H^j(𝒞, -)` of abelian sheaves on `𝒞`.
* `chaoticRightDerivedGlobalSectionsIso` — cohomology on `𝒞` is the right derived functor of
  global sections of `𝒞`, and `chaoticCohomologyFunctorZeroIso` — `H^0(𝒞, -) = Γ(𝒞, -)`.
* `restrictedChaoticCohomologyFunctor` — `F ↦ H^j(𝒞, F|_𝒞)`.

## Main results

* `instIsContinuousWholeι` — the inclusion `𝒞 ⥤ Cris(X/S)` is continuous for the chaotic
  topology on `𝒞`.
* `restrictToWhole_obj_obj` — the sections of `F|_𝒞` over an object of `𝒞` are the sections of
  `F` over that object of `Cris(X/S)`.
* `instAdditiveRestrictToWhole` and `instPreservesFiniteLimitsRestrictToWhole` — the restriction
  is additive and left exact.

## Implementation notes

The subcategory is `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory` of `CrystallineThickening S`,
as the small crystalline site is itself a full subcategory of the big one, so an object carries
its underlying object of `Cris(X/S)` in the field `obj`.  The condition is `IsIso A.obj.toX`
rather than an equality of schemes: the objects of `Cris(X/S)` come with an open immersion
`U ⟶ X`, and "`U = X`" is the statement that it is an isomorphism, which is the only form in
which the condition is stable under the isomorphisms of the category.

The chaotic topology is the bottom Grothendieck topology `⊥`.  That this is the topology
generated by the chaotic pretopology of [Stacks, Tag 07GE] is Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.Pretopology.toGrothendieck_bot`; `sheafEquivPresheaf` below is Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.sheafBotEquivalence` at this site, the other half of that tag.

The cohomology instances are discharged exactly as for `Cris(X/S)`: the objects of `𝒞` form a
`Type (u + 1)` and its morphisms a `Type u`, so the coefficient universe is `u + 1`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07JK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07JK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07GE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07GE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07IG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07IG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03CG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03CG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07JJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07JJ)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Abelian CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite

universe u

noncomputable section

namespace Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite

variable (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u})

/-- The property cutting out the subcategory `𝒞` of [Stacks, Tag 07JK]: the structure map
`U ⟶ X` of an object `(U, T, δ)` of `Cris(X/S)` is an isomorphism, that is, `U` is the whole of
`X`.  The map is always an open immersion, by the definition of the small crystalline site. -/
abbrev IsOverWholeSpace : ObjectProperty (CrystallineThickening S) :=
  fun A ↦ IsIso A.obj.toX

/-- **The category `𝒞` of [Stacks, Tag 07JK]**: the full subcategory of the small crystalline
site `Cris(X/S)` on the divided power thickenings `(X, T, δ)` of the whole of `X`. -/
abbrev WholeSpaceThickening (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}) :=
  (IsOverWholeSpace S).FullSubcategory

/-- The inclusion `𝒞 ⥤ Cris(X/S)` of the thickenings of the whole space into the small
crystalline site. -/
abbrev wholeι : WholeSpaceThickening S ⥤ CrystallineThickening S :=
  (IsOverWholeSpace S).ι

/-- The inclusion `𝒞 ⥤ Cris(X/S)` is fully faithful, being the inclusion of a full
subcategory. -/
abbrev fullyFaithfulWholeι : (wholeι S).FullyFaithful :=
  (IsOverWholeSpace S).fullyFaithfulι

/-- **The chaotic topology on `𝒞`**, as [Stacks, Tag 07JK] prescribes: the bottom Grothendieck
topology, in which only the maximal sieve covers and every presheaf is therefore a sheaf.  That
this is the topology generated by the chaotic pretopology of [Stacks, Tag 07GE] is Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.Pretopology.toGrothendieck_bot`. -/
abbrev chaoticTopology : GrothendieckTopology (WholeSpaceThickening S) := ⊥

/-- **Sheaves on `𝒞` with its chaotic topology are the presheaves on `𝒞`**, the second assertion
of [Stacks, Tag 07GE] at this site. -/
abbrev sheafEquivPresheaf (A : Type*) [Category A] :
    Sheaf (chaoticTopology S) A ≌ (WholeSpaceThickening S)ᵒᵖ ⥤ A :=
  sheafBotEquivalence A

/-- **The inclusion `𝒞 ⥤ Cris(X/S)` is continuous** for the chaotic topology on `𝒞`, so
restriction along it carries sheaves on `Cris(X/S)` to sheaves on `𝒞`. -/
instance instIsContinuousWholeι :
    (wholeι S).IsContinuous (chaoticTopology S) (smallTopology S) :=
  Stacks.ChaoticSite.isContinuous_of_eq_bot _ _ _ rfl

/-- **The restriction `F ↦ F|_𝒞`** of an abelian sheaf on the small crystalline site to the
subcategory `𝒞` of thickenings of the whole space, with its chaotic topology.  This is the
left-hand side of the comparison asserted by [Stacks, Tag 07JK]. -/
abbrev restrictToWhole :
    Sheaf (smallTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} ⥤
      Sheaf (chaoticTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} :=
  (wholeι S).sheafPushforwardContinuous AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}
    (chaoticTopology S) (smallTopology S)

/-- The sections of `F|_𝒞` over an object of `𝒞` are the sections of `F` over the corresponding
object of `Cris(X/S)`. -/
theorem restrictToWhole_obj_obj (F : Sheaf (smallTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})
    (A : WholeSpaceThickening S) :
    ((restrictToWhole S).obj F).obj.obj (op A) = F.obj.obj (op ((wholeι S).obj A)) := rfl

/-- Restriction to `𝒞` is additive. -/
instance instAdditiveRestrictToWhole : (restrictToWhole S).Additive := ⟨rfl⟩

/-- **Restriction to `𝒞` is left exact.** -/
instance instPreservesFiniteLimitsRestrictToWhole :
    PreservesFiniteLimits (restrictToWhole S) :=
  inferInstance

/-! ### Cohomology of the chaotic site `𝒞`

The objects of `𝒞` form a `Type (u + 1)` and its morphisms a `Type u`, so the coefficient
universe is `u + 1`, as for `Cris(X/S)`. -/

/-- Abelian sheaves on `𝒞` admit sheafification, with the coefficients in the universe of the
objects of `𝒞`. -/
instance instHasSheafifyChaotic :
    HasSheafify (chaoticTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} :=
  GrothendieckTopology.hasSheafify_addCommGrpCat.{u + 1, u, u + 1} _

/-- Abelian sheaves on `𝒞` are locally `(u + 1)`-small. -/
instance instLocallySmallChaotic :
    LocallySmall.{u + 1} (Sheaf (chaoticTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}) :=
  Sheaf.locallySmall_of_small.{u + 1, u + 1, u, u + 1, u + 2} (chaoticTopology S)
    AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}

/-- **Abelian sheaves on `𝒞` have enough injectives.** -/
instance instEnoughInjectivesChaotic :
    EnoughInjectives (Sheaf (chaoticTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}) :=
  Sheaf.enoughInjectives_of_small.{u + 1, u + 1, u, u + 1, u + 2} (chaoticTopology S)
    AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}

/-- **`Ext`-groups of abelian sheaves on `𝒞` exist in `Type (u + 1)`.** -/
instance instHasExtChaotic :
    HasExt.{u + 1} (Sheaf (chaoticTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}) :=
  hasExt_of_enoughInjectives.{u + 1} _

/-- **The global sections functor `Γ(𝒞, -)`** of abelian sheaves on `𝒞`. -/
abbrev chaoticGlobalSections :
    Sheaf (chaoticTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} :=
  Sheaf.Γ (chaoticTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}

/-- Global sections of abelian sheaves on `𝒞` are additive. -/
instance instAdditiveChaoticGlobalSections : (chaoticGlobalSections S).Additive :=
  Stacks.Cohomology.GlobalSections.additive_Γ.{u + 1, u, u + 1} (chaoticTopology S)

/-- **The `j`-th cohomology functor `H^j(𝒞, -)`** of abelian sheaves on `𝒞`: the `Ext`-groups in
degree `j` out of the constant sheaf on `ℤ`. -/
def chaoticCohomologyFunctor (j : ℕ) :
    Sheaf (chaoticTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} :=
  Sheaf.functorH.{u + 1, u + 1, u, u + 1} (chaoticTopology S) j

/-- **The cohomology group `H^j(𝒞, F)`** of an abelian sheaf on `𝒞`. -/
abbrev chaoticCohomology (F : Sheaf (chaoticTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}) (j : ℕ) :
    Type (u + 1) :=
  Sheaf.H.{u + 1, u + 1} F j

/-- **Cohomology on `𝒞` is the right derived functor of global sections of `𝒞`**,
`R^j Γ(𝒞, -) ≅ H^j(𝒞, -)`. -/
def chaoticRightDerivedGlobalSectionsIso (j : ℕ) :
    (chaoticGlobalSections S).rightDerived j ≅ chaoticCohomologyFunctor S j :=
  Stacks.Cohomology.GlobalSections.rightDerivedΓIsoFunctorH.{u + 1, u, u + 1}
    (chaoticTopology S) j

/-- **`H^0(𝒞, -) = Γ(𝒞, -)`.** -/
def chaoticCohomologyFunctorZeroIso :
    chaoticCohomologyFunctor S 0 ≅ chaoticGlobalSections S :=
  (chaoticRightDerivedGlobalSectionsIso S 0).symm ≪≫
    (chaoticGlobalSections S).rightDerivedZeroIsoSelf

/-- The cohomology of the restriction `F|_𝒞`, which is the left-hand side of the comparison
asserted by [Stacks, Tag 07JK], read as a functor of `F`. -/
def restrictedChaoticCohomologyFunctor (j : ℕ) :
    Sheaf (smallTopology S) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} :=
  restrictToWhole S ⋙ chaoticCohomologyFunctor S j

end Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite

end

end
